{"term":"identical","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:25821adea9f7982b85","definition":"Bearing full likeness by having precisely the same set of characteristics; indistinguishable.","example":"My car is identical with the one my mom has just bought.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["same"],"antonyms":["contrasting","different","distinct","non-identical","opposite"],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["alloidentical","bioidentical","half-identical","haploidentical","identical by descent","identical by state","identicalism","identicality","identically","identicalness","identical twin","nonidentical","self-identical","semi-identical","semperidentical","unidentical"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/identical#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d6f726a61aa2453fb5","definition":"Not different or other; not another or others; not different as regards self; selfsame; numerically identical.","example":"The best of the joke, too, is, that the very coal-merchant who is loudest in his complaints against the person who defrauded him, is the identical man who sat in the centre of the very front row of the pit last night and laughed the most boisterously at this very same thing,--and not so well done either.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["same","selfsame"],"antonyms":["contrasting","different","distinct","non-identical","opposite"],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["alloidentical","bioidentical","half-identical","haploidentical","identical by descent","identical by state","identicalism","identicality","identically","identicalness","identical twin","nonidentical","self-identical","semi-identical","semperidentical","unidentical"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/identical#English","licens